Third-party code and provenance

upstream/HypCD is unmodified, from https://github.com/Visual-AI/HypCD,
pinned at ffc895b7ff38be8502bb7e3bd851f1d2a55dff73. Source archives include
a hash-verified snapshot of the same commit instead of Git metadata.

The reference losses, hierarchy extraction and evaluation in gcd_runtime/trainer.py,
the objective adapter in crish/loss.py, the shared loop in crish/training.py,
and the USE/SSE arithmetic in crish/rebuild.py derive from
train/train_HypSelEx.py at that commit. Copyright (c) 2025 Visual AI Lab.
The complete MIT notice is retained in LICENSES/HypCD-MIT.txt.

audit/baseline_trace.py loads hashed reference definitions solely for audit/tests.
The reference LabelSmoothingLoss, SupConLoss and info_nce_logits definitions
remain unchanged. CRiSH repair, legal probes and projector lookahead are
experimental extensions; source reuse is not a novelty claim.

gcd_runtime/kmeans.py derives from methods/clustering/faster_mix_k_means_pytorch.py
at the same upstream commit. It preserves the two optimization phases and adds
empty-cluster relocation of unanchored rows, degenerate initialization handling,
device portability, finite-input checks and bounded iteration diagnostics.
These numerical policies are shared by CRiSH and B0, not a new research method.

Backbones, manifold operations, dataset loaders and evaluation helpers are
imported from the pinned upstream source and retain their original notices,
including Meta's notices in the transformer modules. Dependencies and pretrained
weights retain their respective licenses. No datasets or weights are distributed.
